.TH TMENU 1 "November 2026" "dev-workflow-script-bundle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmenu \- interactive terminal command launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmenu
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RI [ JSON_FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmenu
reads a JSON configuration and presents each command as a selectable terminal
item. The selected command is passed to
.BR bash (1)
for execution.
.PP
Use the up and down arrow keys to move through the menu. Press the right arrow
key or Enter to select an item. Press the left arrow key or Ctrl+C to cancel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Collect placeholder values and print the resolved command instead of executing it.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option parsing. The next argument is treated as
.IR JSON_FILE ,
even if it begins with a hyphen.
.SH CONFIGURATION RESOLUTION
.TP
.I JSON_FILE
The optional positional argument.
.TP
.I tmenu.default.json
The bundled fallback file beside
.B tmenu.sh .
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
The configuration must be a JSON array containing menu items with:
.TP
.B name
Required string label shown in the menu.
.TP
.B run
Required string containing the shell command.
.TP
.B confirm
Optional JSON boolean. When true, confirmation is requested before execution.
.PP
The
.I run
value may contain named placeholders in
.B ${variable_name}
form. The menu prompts once for each distinct placeholder, replaces underscores
with spaces in the prompt label, and accepts empty values. Entered text is passed
to Bash as typed. Escape or the left-arrow key aborts placeholder collection and
returns to the menu.
.PP
Bare
.B $variable_name
syntax is invalid. The menu reports the configuration source line and exits with
status 1.
.SH CONFIGURATION SECURITY
The command file must exist, be readable, not be world-writable, and be owned
by the current user or root. Invalid JSON, empty menus, mismatched entries,
unsupported placeholders, and unsafe configuration ownership are rejected.
.PP
Destructive commands and items with
.B confirm
enabled require confirmation. Commands referencing
.B tmenu
itself are allowed, so nested menus can use hierarchical JSON configurations.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use the bundled default configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tmenu
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a use-case configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tmenu /path/to/dev-workflow-script-bundle/src/sh/menu-config-bundle/tmenu.git.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Print a resolved command instead of executing it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tmenu --dry-run commands.json
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I tmenu.sh
Linux implementation in the
.B sh
directory.
.TP
.I tmenu.default.json
Bundled minimal Linux command configuration beside
.B tmenu.sh .
.TP
.I menu-config-bundle/tmenu.git.json
Bundled Git command use-case configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully, or the launcher was canceled.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime/configuration error, invalid arguments, or security refusal occurred.
.TP
.B 130
The launcher was interrupted.
